{"kind":"report","text":"Decision on 03faada8 (planner, 2026-10-20): F1's pass budget and witness 2.\n\n1. No budget change. ARCHIVE_BOUNDS stays as it is (archive-budget.ts:6), with every debit charged, no top-up and no uncharged cache. The note's \"at most 512 retained inputs\" for one pass (sections 2.2, 2.3 rule 6, 2.4 rule 2) is a ceiling. It is not a size that a pass must reach.\n\n2. A pass ends where its budget ends. A pass takes whole entries in order. Its cutoff is the last entry whose full cost fits the budget: the entry, its retained inputs, its reads and its tree work. The pass then confirms what it wrote, and the next pass starts at the next entry. No entry is lost or written twice. A pass always takes at least one whole entry. If one entry alone does not fit, the pass stops with limit, as A3 does today, and the archive reports it.\n\n3. Witness 2 changes. Its middle part said \"nine passes each add 512 new retained inputs\". It now reads: passes add new retained inputs of one kind, each pass as many as the unchanged budget admits, until the archive holds more than 4,608 retained files. Then one more pass adds one. The assertions stay: one retained file in that pass's own directory, no earlier retained path changes, and the tree probe within the bound of rule 7. Two assertions are added. Each of those passes ends at an entry boundary because of the budget. The next pass starts at the following entry. The restart part of witness 2 does not change. This decision amends the note's witness 2; a later planner head corrects its text.\n\n4. Full pipeline. Witness 2 passes only through the native export path: the real ArchiveBudget, the native entry and retained-input reads, and the inventory debits. The 4,608-file tree-mechanics run and the minimum-debit diagnostic stay as findings. Neither is witness 2.\n\n5. Throughput, for slice 9. One attempt per entry means one pass covers at most 512 entries, and fewer when entries name new retained inputs. F1's report states the entries per pass that the Grow fixture reaches. Slice 9 sets the pass cadence from that figure so that the archive gains on Room A, at about 4,800 entries a day, by at least three times, and states the catch-up time from position 0.\n\nNo deployment.","body":{"to":"builder"}}